    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a difficult slate today as our core hitters are stifled by elite opposing arms, leaving our efficiency scores tightly clustered in the \"marginal\" range. **Kyle Schwarber** earns the top projection of the day at 52.14, largely buoyed by a lead-off spot against Cease. While the 2.96 xERA of the opposition suggests a suppressed ceiling, **Kyle Schwarber** benefits from a +10% order adjustment, making him our safest bet for R and HR production. **Junior Caminero** follows closely at 50.32; despite a negative platoon split against S\u00e1nchez, his 0.374 xwOBA provides enough underlying quality to justify his start in the 4-hole. **Yordan Alvarez** rounds out our active bats at 49.70; though his L/L matchup is suboptimal, his elite 0.476 xwOBA remains our most potent weapon, and he retains value due to his position at #2 in the order.\n\nNavigating this roster has been difficult due to an off-day for our speed-oriented depth. With **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Caleb Durbin** all inactive today, our stolen base category is essentially static, placing the onus on our starters to produce volume in the remaining categories. Given the lack of high-scoring bench options\u2014most of whom, such as **Hyeseong Kim**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Colt Keith**, and **Carson Benge**, are facing similarly difficult pitching rotations or sitting\u2014we are leaning into our primary starters to manage daily game caps. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez**, **Luke Raley**, and **Lars Nootbaar** closely; should any of them be pulled from the lineup or if weather risks emerge, we will look to defensive substitutions like **Casey Schmitt** or **Dillon Dingler**. \n\nRisk management is the priority today, as the entire active lineup is facing pitchers with xERAs under 3.00. We are particularly concerned about the stagnant production from the lower-tier utility players like **Nelson Velazquez**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase 